IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ea-core`

-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation
-- "version in force from 5/12/2025" -- THE KEEL'S DEFINITIONS: s 2(1) in full,
-- and ss 3(1), 5 and 6 (the other provisions of lines 1-784 are inert or blank:
-- see NOTES.md, coverage table).
--
-- Source text: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore
-- Statutes Online (inputs/EmA1968.txt).  It is not the official text.  Every
-- `-- src:` line copies a line of that file; every quotation in a FALSE-kind
-- comment is a phrase of it.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  A definition is asked of a case ("is this person an
-- employee?").  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act itself gives;
-- NOTHING means the Act does not answer on these facts.  Never read NOTHING as no.
--   * a "means" definition answers JUST FALSE for a case outside it, in the words
--     "means ...";
--   * a "means ... and includes ..." definition answers JUST TRUE inside either
--     limb and NOTHING outside both (the word "includes" opens the list);
--   * an "includes" definition answers JUST TRUE for the listed things and NOTHING
--     for anything else;
--   * a pointer to another Act ("has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the
--     Employment Claims Act 2016") takes the other Act's answer as a MAYBE input
--     and passes a NOTHING on.
-- Every input is a plain fact a witness could state, or an answer another part of
-- the Act gives (a MAYBE input), or something the Act hands to the Minister or the
-- President (a plain BOOLEAN input that says whether the declaration was made).
-- The opening words of s 2(1), "unless the context otherwise requires", are not
-- encoded as a condition: no input could say what the context requires (NOTES.md,
-- fork F1).

§ `Employment Act 1968 -- Part 1 Preliminary`

§§ `s 2(1) Interpretation: the money terms`

-- The three pay terms count different items of the same record (`Pay for a period`,
-- in ea-core).  "The total amount of money" for the basic rate and the gross rate
-- is the money the contract pays for working for the period: the first ten items
-- of the record.  The six items that are not money paid for working (value of an
-- amenity, a service excluded by order, a travelling concession, the employer's own
-- contributions, a gratuity, a retrenchment benefit) are left out of it (NOTES.md,
-- fork F4).
-- src:363 | “basic rate of pay” means the total amount of money (including
-- src:364 | wage adjustments and increments) to which an employee is
-- src:365 | entitled under his or her contract of service either for working
-- src:366 | for a period of time, that is, for one hour, one day, one week,
-- src:367 | one month or for such other period as may be stated or
-- src:368 | implied in his or her contract of service, or for each
-- src:369 | completed piece or task of work but does not include —
-- src:371 | (a) additional payments by way of overtime payments;
-- src:373 | (b) additional payments by way of bonus payments or
-- src:374 | annual wage supplements;
-- src:376 | (c) any sum paid to the employee to reimburse him or her
-- src:377 | for special expenses incurred by him or her in the
-- src:378 | course of his or her employment;
-- src:380 | (d) productivity incentive payments; and
-- src:382 | (e) any allowance however described;
@ref s 2(1) "basic rate of pay" (src:363-382)
GIVEN pay IS A `Pay for a period`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2(1) "basic rate of pay" the amount` MEANS
    -- the total amount of money entitled for working, including wage adjustments and increments
    sum (LIST
            pay's `pay for the work, with wage adjustments and increments`
          , pay's `overtime payments`
          , pay's `bonus payments or annual wage supplements`
          , pay's `commissions`
          , pay's `productivity incentive payments`
          , pay's `sums paid to reimburse special expenses incurred in the course of employment`
          , pay's `travelling allowances`
          , pay's `food allowances`
          , pay's `housing allowances`
          , pay's `allowances of any other kind`
         )
    MINUS
    -- but does not include (a) overtime payments, (b) bonus payments or annual wage supplements, (c) reimbursement of special expenses, (d) productivity incentive payments, (e) any allowance however described
    sum (LIST
            pay's `overtime payments`
          , pay's `bonus payments or annual wage supplements`
          , pay's `sums paid to reimburse special expenses incurred in the course of employment`
          , pay's `productivity incentive payments`
          , pay's `travelling allowances`
          , pay's `food allowances`
          , pay's `housing allowances`
          , pay's `allowances of any other kind`
         )

-- src:483 | “gross rate of pay” means the total amount of money including
-- src:484 | allowances to which an employee is entitled under his or her
-- src:485 | contract of service either for working for a period of time,
-- src:486 | that is, for one hour, one day, one week, one month or for such
-- src:487 | other period as may be stated or implied in his or her contract
-- src:488 | of service, or for each completed piece or task of work but
-- src:489 | does not include —
-- src:494 | (a) additional payments by way of overtime payments;
-- src:496 | (b) additional payments by way of bonus payments or
-- src:497 | annual wage supplements;
-- src:499 | (c) any sum paid to the employee to reimburse him or her
-- src:500 | for special expenses incurred by him or her in the
-- src:501 | course of his or her employment;
-- src:503 | (d) productivity incentive payments; and
-- src:505 | (e) travelling, food or housing allowances;
@ref s 2(1) "gross rate of pay" (src:483-505)
GIVEN pay IS A `Pay for a period`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2(1) "gross rate of pay" the amount` MEANS
    -- the total amount of money, including allowances, entitled for working
    sum (LIST
            pay's `pay for the work, with wage adjustments and increments`
          , pay's `overtime payments`
          , pay's `bonus payments or annual wage supplements`
          , pay's `commissions`
          , pay's `productivity incentive payments`
          , pay's `sums paid to reimburse special expenses incurred in the course of employment`
          , pay's `travelling allowances`
          , pay's `food allowances`
          , pay's `housing allowances`
          , pay's `allowances of any other kind`
         )
    MINUS
    -- but does not include (a) overtime payments, (b) bonus payments or annual wage supplements, (c) reimbursement of special expenses, (d) productivity incentive payments, (e) travelling, food or housing allowances
    sum (LIST
            pay's `overtime payments`
          , pay's `bonus payments or annual wage supplements`
          , pay's `sums paid to reimburse special expenses incurred in the course of employment`
          , pay's `productivity incentive payments`
          , pay's `travelling allowances`
          , pay's `food allowances`
          , pay's `housing allowances`
         )

-- src:605 | “salary” means all remuneration including allowances payable
-- src:606 | to an employee in respect of work done under his or her
-- src:607 | contract of service, but does not include —
-- src:609 | (a) the value of any house accommodation, supply of
-- src:610 | electricity, water, medical attendance, or other
-- src:611 | amenity, or of any service excluded by general or
-- src:612 | special order of the Minister published in the Gazette;
-- src:614 | (b) any contribution paid by the employer on his or her
-- src:615 | own account to any pension fund or provident fund;
-- src:617 | (c) any travelling allowance or the value of any
-- src:618 | travelling concession;
-- src:620 | (d) any sum paid to the employee to reimburse him or her
-- src:621 | for special expenses incurred by him or her in the
-- src:622 | course of his or her employment;
-- src:624 | (e) any gratuity payable on discharge or retirement; and
-- src:626 | (f) any retrenchment benefit payable on retrenchment;
@ref s 2(1) "salary" (src:605-626)
GIVEN pay IS A `Pay for a period`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2(1) "salary" the amount` MEANS
    -- all remuneration including allowances payable in respect of work done
    sum (LIST
            pay's `pay for the work, with wage adjustments and increments`
          , pay's `overtime payments`
          , pay's `bonus payments or annual wage supplements`
          , pay's `commissions`
          , pay's `productivity incentive payments`
          , pay's `sums paid to reimburse special expenses incurred in the course of employment`
          , pay's `travelling allowances`
          , pay's `food allowances`
          , pay's `housing allowances`
          , pay's `allowances of any other kind`
          , pay's `value of house accommodation, electricity, water, medical attendance or other amenity`
          , pay's `value of a service excluded by order of the Minister`
          , pay's `value of a travelling concession`
          , pay's `employer's contributions on its own account to a pension fund or provident fund`
          , pay's `gratuity payable on discharge or retirement`
          , pay's `retrenchment benefit payable on retrenchment`
         )
    MINUS
    -- but does not include (a) the value of an amenity or of a service excluded by order, (b) the employer's own contribution to a pension or provident fund, (c) a travelling allowance or the value of a travelling concession, (d) reimbursement of special expenses, (e) a gratuity, (f) a retrenchment benefit
    sum (LIST
            pay's `value of house accommodation, electricity, water, medical attendance or other amenity`
          , pay's `value of a service excluded by order of the Minister`
          , pay's `employer's contributions on its own account to a pension fund or provident fund`
          , pay's `travelling allowances`
          , pay's `value of a travelling concession`
          , pay's `sums paid to reimburse special expenses incurred in the course of employment`
          , pay's `gratuity payable on discharge or retirement`
          , pay's `retrenchment benefit payable on retrenchment`
         )

-- src:672 | “wages” means salary;
@ref s 2(1) "wages" (src:672)
GIVEN pay IS A `Pay for a period`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2(1) "wages" the amount` MEANS `s 2(1) "salary" the amount` pay

-- src:582 | “productivity incentive payment” means a variable payment,
-- src:583 | whether made annually or otherwise, to an employee as a
-- src:584 | reward for —
-- src:586 | (a) an improvement to the employee’s performance; or
-- src:591 | (b) an increase in the employee’s productivity or
-- src:592 | contribution to the employer’s business, trade or
-- src:593 | undertaking,
-- src:595 | but does not include any payment which forms part of the
-- src:596 | employee’s regular remuneration;
@ref s 2(1) "productivity incentive payment" (src:582-596)
GIVEN `it is a variable payment, whether made annually or otherwise, to an employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it rewards an improvement to the employee's performance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it rewards an increase in the employee's productivity or contribution to the employer's business, trade or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it forms part of the employee's regular remuneration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "productivity incentive payment" the payment is one` MEANS
    IF `it is a variable payment, whether made annually or otherwise, to an employee` AND (`it rewards an improvement to the employee's performance` OR `it rewards an increase in the employee's productivity or contribution to the employer's business, trade or undertaking`) AND (NOT `it forms part of the employee's regular remuneration`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a variable payment, whether made annually or otherwise, to an employee as a reward for"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 2(1) Interpretation: time`

-- src:423 | “day” means a period of 24 hours beginning at midnight;
@ref s 2(1) "day" (src:423)
GIVEN `the length of the period in hours` IS A NUMBER
      `the period begins at midnight` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "day" the period is a day` MEANS
    IF (`the length of the period in hours` EQUALS 24) AND `the period begins at midnight`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a period of 24 hours beginning at midnight"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:674 | “week” means a continuous period of 7 days;
@ref s 2(1) "week" (src:674)
GIVEN `the number of days in the period` IS A NUMBER
      `the period is continuous` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "week" the period is a week` MEANS
    IF (`the number of days in the period` EQUALS 7) AND `the period is continuous`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a continuous period of 7 days"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The time the employee is at the employer's disposal and not free, less the
-- intervals allowed for rest and meals that fall within it.
-- src:507 | “hours of work” means the time during which an employee is at
-- src:508 | the employer’s disposal and is not free to dispose of his or her
-- src:509 | own time and movements exclusive of any intervals allowed
-- src:510 | for rest and meals;
@ref s 2(1) "hours of work" (src:507-510)
GIVEN `hours at the employer's disposal and not free to dispose of own time and movements` IS A NUMBER
      `hours of intervals allowed for rest and meals within those hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2(1) "hours of work" the number of hours` MEANS
    `hours at the employer's disposal and not free to dispose of own time and movements` MINUS `hours of intervals allowed for rest and meals within those hours`

-- "Overtime" is the hours over "the limits specified in Part 4".  The limit is
-- Part 4's own answer (s 38(1) or s 40(1)): it is a MAYBE input, and a NOTHING
-- from Part 4 is passed on.
-- src:569 | “overtime” means the number of hours worked in any one day or
-- src:570 | in any one week in excess of the limits specified in Part 4;
@ref s 2(1) "overtime" (src:569-570)
GIVEN `the hours worked in the day or the week` IS A NUMBER
      `the limit of hours specified in Part 4 for that day or week` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2(1) "overtime" the number of hours` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the limit of hours specified in Part 4 for that day or week`
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the limit is the answer of Part 4 and Part 4 gave none for these facts
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST limit THEN JUST (IF `the hours worked in the day or the week` GREATER THAN limit THEN `the hours worked in the day or the week` MINUS limit ELSE 0)

§§ `s 2(1) Interpretation: the persons`

-- src:360 | “authorised officer” means any public officer appointed as an
-- src:361 | authorised officer under section 3(2);
@ref s 2(1) "authorised officer" (src:360-361)
GIVEN `the person is a public officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is appointed as an authorised officer under section 3(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "authorised officer" the person is one` MEANS
    IF `the person is a public officer` AND `the person is appointed as an authorised officer under section 3(2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any public officer appointed as an authorised officer under section 3(2)"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:533 | “inspecting officer” means any person appointed as an
-- src:534 | inspecting officer under section 3(2);
@ref s 2(1) "inspecting officer" (src:533-534)
GIVEN `the person is appointed as an inspecting officer under section 3(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "inspecting officer" the person is one` MEANS
    IF `the person is appointed as an inspecting officer under section 3(2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any person appointed as an inspecting officer under section 3(2)"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- (a) a medical practitioner employed by the Government or an approved medical
-- institution, or (b) any other medical practitioner whom the Minister declares.
-- src:552 | “medical officer” means —
-- src:554 | (a) a medical practitioner employed by the Government
-- src:555 | or an approved medical institution; or
-- src:557 | (b) any other medical practitioner whom the Minister
-- src:558 | declares, by notification in the Gazette, to be a
-- src:559 | medical officer for the purposes of this Act;
@ref s 2(1) "medical officer" (src:552-559)
GIVEN `the person is a medical practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is employed by the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is employed by an approved medical institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has, by notification in the Gazette, declared the person a medical officer for the purposes of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "medical officer" the person is one` MEANS
    IF `the person is a medical practitioner` AND (`the person is employed by the Government` OR `the person is employed by an approved medical institution` OR `the Minister has, by notification in the Gazette, declared the person a medical officer for the purposes of this Act`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“medical officer” means —"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:561 | “medical practitioner” means a medical practitioner registered
-- src:562 | under the Medical Registration Act 1997, and includes a
-- src:563 | dentist registered under the Dental Registration Act 1999;
@ref s 2(1) "medical practitioner" (src:561-563)
GIVEN `the person is registered under the Medical Registration Act 1997` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a dentist registered under the Dental Registration Act 1999` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "medical practitioner" the person is one` MEANS
    IF `the person is registered under the Medical Registration Act 1997` OR `the person is a dentist registered under the Dental Registration Act 1999`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "means a medical practitioner registered under the Medical Registration Act 1997, and includes a dentist registered under the Dental Registration Act 1999" opens the class, and a person registered under neither Act is not said to be outside it
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:355 | “approved medical institution” means a hospital, clinic,
-- src:356 | healthcare establishment or other medical institution which
-- src:357 | the Minister, by notification in the Gazette, declares as an
-- src:358 | approved medical institution;
@ref s 2(1) "approved medical institution" (src:355-358)
GIVEN `it is a hospital, clinic, healthcare establishment or other medical institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has, by notification in the Gazette, declared it an approved medical institution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "approved medical institution" the institution is one` MEANS
    IF `it is a hospital, clinic, healthcare establishment or other medical institution` AND `the Minister has, by notification in the Gazette, declared it an approved medical institution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a hospital, clinic, healthcare establishment or other medical institution which the Minister, by notification in the Gazette, declares as an approved medical institution"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The members of the family named, by their relationship to the employee.  An
-- adopted or illegitimate child counts only if living with or dependent on the
-- employee.  "Child" is not defined in s 2(1): a stepchild or a child the employee
-- fosters is neither named nor excluded.
-- src:425 | “dependant” means any of the following members of an
-- src:426 | employee’s family, namely, wife, husband, father, mother,
-- src:427 | child and any adopted or illegitimate child living with or
-- src:428 | dependent on the employee;
@ref s 2(1) "dependant" (src:425-428)
GIVEN member IS A `Family member of the employee`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "dependant" the member of the family is one` MEANS
    CONSIDER member's `relationship`
    WHEN `Relationship: the employee's wife` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Relationship: the employee's husband` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Relationship: the employee's father` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Relationship: the employee's mother` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Relationship: the employee's child` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Relationship: the employee's adopted child` THEN
        IF member's `lives with the employee` OR member's `is dependent on the employee`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any adopted or illegitimate child living with or dependent on the employee"
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `Relationship: the employee's illegitimate child` THEN
        IF member's `lives with the employee` OR member's `is dependent on the employee`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any adopted or illegitimate child living with or dependent on the employee"
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): s 2(1) does not define "child", so it does not say whether the employee's stepchild is the employee's "child"
    WHEN `Relationship: the employee's stepchild` THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): s 2(1) does not define "child", so it does not say whether a child the employee fosters is the employee's "child"
    WHEN `Relationship: a child the employee fosters` THEN NOTHING
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any of the following members of an employee's family, namely"
    WHEN `Relationship: no relationship the Act names` THEN JUST FALSE

-- src:439 | “domestic worker” means any house, stable or garden servant or
-- src:440 | motor car driver, employed in or in connection with the
-- src:441 | domestic services of any private premises;
@ref s 2(1) "domestic worker" (src:439-441)
DECLARE `s 2(1) "domestic worker" Kind of work` IS ONE OF
    `s 2(1) "domestic worker" work as a house servant`
    `s 2(1) "domestic worker" work as a stable servant`
    `s 2(1) "domestic worker" work as a garden servant`
    `s 2(1) "domestic worker" work as a motor car driver`
    `s 2(1) "domestic worker" work of some other kind`

@ref s 2(1) "domestic worker" (src:439-441)
GIVEN work IS A `s 2(1) "domestic worker" Kind of work`
      `the person is employed in or in connection with the domestic services of private premises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "domestic worker" the person is one` MEANS
    IF `the person is employed in or in connection with the domestic services of private premises` AND (work EQUALS `s 2(1) "domestic worker" work as a house servant` OR work EQUALS `s 2(1) "domestic worker" work as a stable servant` OR work EQUALS `s 2(1) "domestic worker" work as a garden servant` OR work EQUALS `s 2(1) "domestic worker" work as a motor car driver`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any house, stable or garden servant or motor car driver, employed in or in connection with the domestic services of any private premises"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- Facts about work on board a ship.  A harbour craft or pleasure craft is covered
-- only when licensed under regulations made under s 41 of the Maritime and Port
-- Authority of Singapore Act 1996 and used within a port declared under s 3 of
-- that Act (borrowed facts, asked as one input).
-- src:628 | “seafarer” means any person, including the master, who is
-- src:629 | employed or engaged or works in any capacity on board a
-- src:630 | ship, but does not include —
-- src:632 | (a) a pilot;
-- src:634 | (b) a port worker;
-- src:639 | (c) a person temporarily employed on the ship during the
-- src:640 | period it is in port; and
-- src:642 | (d) a person who is employed or engaged or works in any
-- src:643 | capacity on board a harbour craft or pleasure craft
-- src:644 | licensed under regulations made under section 41 of
-- src:645 | the Maritime and Port Authority of Singapore
-- src:646 | Act 1996, when the harbour craft or pleasure craft
-- src:647 | is used within a port declared by the Minister under
-- src:648 | section 3 of that Act;
@ref s 2(1) "seafarer" (src:628-648)
GIVEN `the person is employed or engaged or works in any capacity on board a ship, including as its master` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a pilot` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a port worker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is temporarily employed on the ship during the period it is in port` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person works on board a licensed harbour craft or pleasure craft used within a declared port` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "seafarer" the person is one` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include"
        IF `the person is a pilot` OR `the person is a port worker` OR `the person is temporarily employed on the ship during the period it is in port` OR `the person works on board a licensed harbour craft or pleasure craft used within a declared port` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the person is employed or engaged or works in any capacity on board a ship, including as its master` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any person, including the master, who is employed or engaged or works in any capacity on board a ship"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- The persons the Act deals with in Part 6.
-- src:418 | “contractor” means any person who contracts with a principal to
-- src:419 | supply labour or to carry out the whole or any part of any
-- src:420 | work undertaken by the principal in the course of or for the
-- src:421 | purposes of the principal’s trade or business;
@ref s 2(1) "contractor" (src:418-421)
GIVEN `the person contracts with a principal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is to supply labour or to carry out the whole or any part of work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work is undertaken by the principal in the course of or for the purposes of the principal's trade or business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "contractor" the person is one` MEANS
    IF `the person contracts with a principal` AND `the contract is to supply labour or to carry out the whole or any part of work` AND `the work is undertaken by the principal in the course of or for the purposes of the principal's trade or business`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any person who contracts with a principal to supply labour or to carry out the whole or any part of any work undertaken by the principal"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:576 | “principal” means any person who, in the course of or for the
-- src:577 | purposes of the person’s trade or business, contracts with a
-- src:578 | contractor for the supply of labour or for the execution by the
-- src:579 | contractor of the whole or any part of any work undertaken by
-- src:580 | the principal;
@ref s 2(1) "principal" (src:576-580)
GIVEN `the person acts in the course of or for the purposes of the person's trade or business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person contracts with a contractor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is for the supply of labour or for the execution by the contractor of the whole or any part of work undertaken by the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "principal" the person is one` MEANS
    IF `the person acts in the course of or for the purposes of the person's trade or business` AND `the person contracts with a contractor` AND `the contract is for the supply of labour or for the execution by the contractor of the whole or any part of work undertaken by the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any person who, in the course of or for the purposes of the person's trade or business, contracts with a contractor"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:655 | “subcontractor” means any person who contracts with a
-- src:656 | contractor for the supply of labour or for the execution by
-- src:657 | the subcontractor of the whole or any part of any work
-- src:658 | undertaken by the contractor for the contractor’s principal,
-- src:659 | and includes any person who contracts with a subcontractor
-- src:660 | to supply labour or to carry out the whole or any part of any
-- src:661 | work undertaken by the subcontractor for a contractor;
@ref s 2(1) "subcontractor" (src:655-661)
GIVEN `the person contracts with a contractor for the supply of labour or for the execution by the person of the whole or any part of work undertaken by the contractor for the contractor's principal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person contracts with a subcontractor to supply labour or to carry out the whole or any part of work undertaken by the subcontractor for a contractor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "subcontractor" the person is one` MEANS
    IF `the person contracts with a contractor for the supply of labour or for the execution by the person of the whole or any part of work undertaken by the contractor for the contractor's principal` OR `the person contracts with a subcontractor to supply labour or to carry out the whole or any part of work undertaken by the subcontractor for a contractor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "means any person who contracts with a contractor ... and includes any person who contracts with a subcontractor" opens the class beyond the two kinds of contract it names
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:663 | “subcontractor for labour” means any person who contracts with
-- src:664 | a contractor or subcontractor to supply the labour required for
-- src:665 | the execution of the whole or any part of any work a
-- src:666 | contractor or subcontractor has contracted to carry out for a
-- src:667 | principal or contractor, as the case may be;
@ref s 2(1) "subcontractor for labour" (src:663-667)
GIVEN `the person contracts with a contractor or a subcontractor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is to supply the labour required for the execution of the whole or any part of work that contractor or subcontractor has contracted to carry out for a principal or contractor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "subcontractor for labour" the person is one` MEANS
    IF `the person contracts with a contractor or a subcontractor` AND `the contract is to supply the labour required for the execution of the whole or any part of work that contractor or subcontractor has contracted to carry out for a principal or contractor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any person who contracts with a contractor or subcontractor to supply the labour required"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- Building and civil engineering work, with repair, maintenance, alteration and
-- demolition work added.
-- src:408 | “constructional work” means any building and civil engineering
-- src:409 | work and includes repair, maintenance, alteration and
-- src:410 | demolition work;
@ref s 2(1) "constructional work" (src:408-410)
GIVEN `it is building work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is civil engineering work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is repair, maintenance, alteration or demolition work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "constructional work" the work is constructional work` MEANS
    IF `it is building work` OR `it is civil engineering work` OR `it is repair, maintenance, alteration or demolition work`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "means any building and civil engineering work and includes repair, maintenance, alteration and demolition work" opens the class
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:393 | “constructional contractor” means any person, firm, corporation
-- src:394 | or company who or which is established for the purpose of
-- src:395 | undertaking, either exclusively or in addition to or in
-- src:396 | conjunction with any other business, any type of
-- src:401 | constructional work, and who or which is carrying out the
-- src:402 | constructional work for or on behalf of some other person
-- src:403 | under a contract entered into by that person, firm, corporation
-- src:404 | or company with such other person, and includes heirs,
-- src:405 | executors, administrators, assigns and successors of that
-- src:406 | person, firm, corporation or company;
@ref s 2(1) "constructional contractor" (src:393-406)
GIVEN `the person is a person, firm, corporation or company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is established for the purpose of undertaking, exclusively or with other business, a type of constructional work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is carrying out constructional work for or on behalf of some other person under a contract with that person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an heir, executor, administrator, assign or successor of such a person, firm, corporation or company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "constructional contractor" the person is one` MEANS
    IF (`the person is a person, firm, corporation or company` AND `it is established for the purpose of undertaking, exclusively or with other business, a type of constructional work` AND `it is carrying out constructional work for or on behalf of some other person under a contract with that person`) OR `it is an heir, executor, administrator, assign or successor of such a person, firm, corporation or company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "and includes heirs, executors, administrators, assigns and successors" opens the class beyond the person who is carrying out the work
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 2(1) Interpretation: the contract, employee and employer`

-- src:412 | “contract of service” means any agreement, whether written or
-- src:413 | oral, express or implied, whereby one person agrees to
-- src:414 | employ another as an employee and that other agrees to serve
-- src:415 | his or her employer as an employee and includes an
-- src:416 | apprenticeship contract or agreement;
@ref s 2(1) "contract of service" (src:412-416)
GIVEN `there is an agreement, whether written or oral, express or implied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one person agrees to employ another as an employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that other agrees to serve the first as an employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an apprenticeship contract or agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "contract of service" the agreement is one` MEANS
    IF (`there is an agreement, whether written or oral, express or implied` AND `one person agrees to employ another as an employee` AND `that other agrees to serve the first as an employee`) OR `it is an apprenticeship contract or agreement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "means any agreement ... and includes an apprenticeship contract or agreement" opens the class
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The Act's "workman" has five limbs and a proviso that deems a person a workman.
-- Limb (d) is the First Schedule and limb (a) leaves out a seafarer and a domestic
-- worker.  The proviso compares, for every salary period (s 20), the time required
-- as a workman with the total time required.
-- src:676 | “workman” means —
-- src:678 | (a) any person, skilled or unskilled, who has entered into
-- src:679 | a contract of service with an employer pursuant to
-- src:680 | which he or she is engaged in manual labour,
-- src:681 | including any artisan or apprentice, but excluding
-- src:682 | any seafarer or domestic worker;
-- src:687 | (b) any person, other than clerical staff, employed in the
-- src:688 | operation or maintenance of mechanically‑propelled
-- src:689 | vehicles used for the transport of passengers for hire
-- src:690 | or for commercial purposes;
-- src:692 | (c) any person employed partly for manual labour and
-- src:693 | partly for the purpose of supervising in person any
-- src:694 | workman in and throughout the performance of his or
-- src:695 | her work:
-- src:697 | Provided that when any person is employed by any
-- src:698 | one employer partly as a workman and partly in some other
-- src:699 | capacity or capacities, that person is deemed to be a
-- src:700 | workman unless it can be established that the time during
-- src:701 | which that workman has been required to work as a
-- src:702 | workman in any one salary period as defined in Part 3 has
-- src:703 | on no occasion amounted to or exceeded one‑half of the
-- src:704 | total time during which that person has been required to
-- src:705 | work in such salary period;
-- src:707 | (d) any person specified in the First Schedule; or
-- src:709 | (e) any person whom the Minister may, by notification in
-- src:710 | the Gazette, declare to be a workman for the purposes
-- src:711 | of this Act.
@ref s 2(1) "workman" (src:676-711)
DECLARE `s 2(1) "workman" Time in one salary period` HAS
    `time the person was required to work as a workman` IS A NUMBER
    `total time the person was required to work` IS A NUMBER

@ref s 2(1) "workman" (src:697-705)
GIVEN `the person is employed partly as a workman and partly in some other capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      periods IS A LIST OF `s 2(1) "workman" Time in one salary period`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "workman" proviso: the person is deemed to be a workman` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the proviso deems a workman only a person employed partly as a workman and partly in another capacity
        IF NOT `the person is employed partly as a workman and partly in some other capacity` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless it can be established that the time during which that workman has been required to work as a workman in any one salary period"
        IF `it is established that on no occasion did the workman time reach one-half` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `it is established that on no occasion did the workman time reach one-half` MEANS
            (NOT (null periods)) AND all (GIVEN period YIELD period's `time the person was required to work as a workman` LESS THAN (period's `total time the person was required to work` DIVIDED BY 2)) periods

@ref s 2(1) "workman" (src:676-711)
GIVEN `the person is engaged in manual labour under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a seafarer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a domestic worker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is employed in the operation or maintenance of mechanically-propelled vehicles used for the transport of passengers for hire or for commercial purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is clerical staff` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is employed partly for manual labour and partly for the purpose of supervising in person any workman in and throughout the performance of the person's work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the First Schedule specifies the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has, by notification in the Gazette, declared the person a workman` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proviso deems the person a workman` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "workman" the person is one` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the person is engaged in manual labour under a contract of service` AND (NOT `the person is a seafarer`) AND (NOT `the person is a domestic worker`)) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the person is employed in the operation or maintenance of mechanically-propelled vehicles used for the transport of passengers for hire or for commercial purposes` AND (NOT `the person is clerical staff`)) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person is employed partly for manual labour and partly for the purpose of supervising in person any workman in and throughout the performance of the person's work` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the Minister has, by notification in the Gazette, declared the person a workman` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the proviso deems the person a workman` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the First Schedule specifies the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): limb (d) is the First Schedule's answer, and the First Schedule gave none for these facts
        IF `the First Schedule specifies the person` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“workman” means —"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:446 | “employee” means a person who has entered into or works under
-- src:447 | a contract of service with an employer and includes a
-- src:448 | workman, and any officer or employee of the Government
-- src:449 | included in a category, class or description of such officers or
-- src:450 | employees declared by the President to be employees for the
-- src:451 | purposes of this Act or any provision thereof, but does not
-- src:452 | include any of the following:
-- src:454 | (a) any seafarer;
-- src:456 | (b) any domestic worker;
-- src:458 | (c) [Deleted by Act 55 of 2018]
-- src:460 | (d) any person belonging to any other class of persons
-- src:461 | whom the Minister may, by notification in the
-- src:462 | Gazette, declare not to be employees for the
-- src:463 | purposes of this Act;
@ref s 2(1) "employee" (src:446-463)
GIVEN `the person has entered into a contract of service with an employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person works under a contract of service with an employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a workman` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer or employee of the Government in a category, class or description declared by the President to be employees for the purposes of this Act or a provision of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a seafarer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a domestic worker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person belongs to a class the Minister has, by notification in the Gazette, declared not to be employees for the purposes of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "employee" the person is one` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include any of the following"
        IF `the person is a seafarer` OR `the person is a domestic worker` OR `the person belongs to a class the Minister has, by notification in the Gazette, declared not to be employees for the purposes of this Act` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the person has entered into a contract of service with an employer` OR `the person works under a contract of service with an employer` OR `the person is a workman` OR `the person is an officer or employee of the Government in a category, class or description declared by the President to be employees for the purposes of this Act or a provision of it` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "means a person who has entered into or works under a contract of service with an employer and includes a workman, and any officer or employee of the Government" opens the class
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:465 | “employer” means any person who employs another person
-- src:466 | under a contract of service and includes —
-- src:468 | (a) the Government in respect of such categories, classes
-- src:469 | or descriptions of officers or employees of the
-- src:470 | Government as are declared by the President to be
-- src:471 | employees for the purposes of this Act;
-- src:473 | (b) any statutory authority;
-- src:475 | (c) the duly authorised agent or manager of the
-- src:476 | employer; and
-- src:478 | (d) the person who owns or is carrying on or for the time
-- src:479 | being responsible for the management of the
-- src:480 | profession, business, trade or work in which the
-- src:481 | employee is engaged;
@ref s 2(1) "employer" (src:465-481)
GIVEN `the person employs another person under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Government and the employee is in a category, class or description declared by the President to be employees for the purposes of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a statutory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the duly authorised agent or manager of the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person owns or is carrying on or for the time being is responsible for the management of the profession, business, trade or work in which the employee is engaged` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "employer" the person is one` MEANS
    IF `the person employs another person under a contract of service` OR `the person is the Government and the employee is in a category, class or description declared by the President to be employees for the purposes of this Act` OR `the person is a statutory authority` OR `the person is the duly authorised agent or manager of the employer` OR `the person owns or is carrying on or for the time being is responsible for the management of the profession, business, trade or work in which the employee is engaged`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "means any person who employs another person under a contract of service and includes" opens the class
    ELSE NOTHING

-- "Dismiss" includes a forced resignation if the employee can show it.
-- src:430 | “dismiss” means to terminate the contract of service between an
-- src:431 | employer and an employee at the employer’s initiative, with
-- src:432 | or without notice and for cause or otherwise, and includes the
-- src:433 | resignation of an employee if the employee can show, on a
-- src:434 | balance of probabilities, that the employee did not resign
-- src:435 | voluntarily but was forced to do so because of any conduct or
-- src:436 | omission, or course of conduct or omissions, engaged in by
-- src:437 | the employer;
@ref s 2(1) "dismiss" (src:430-437)
GIVEN `the contract of service has been terminated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was terminated at the employer's initiative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee resigned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee can show, on a balance of probabilities, that the employee did not resign voluntarily but was forced to do so because of conduct or omissions of the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "dismiss" the ending of the contract is a dismissal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the contract of service has been terminated` AND `it was terminated at the employer's initiative` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the employee resigned` AND `the employee can show, on a balance of probabilities, that the employee did not resign voluntarily but was forced to do so because of conduct or omissions of the employer` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "includes the resignation of an employee if the employee can show" (a failed "if" is the text's no, marginal reading (a); NOTES.md, fork F5)
        IF `the employee resigned` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "means to terminate the contract of service between an employer and an employee at the employer's initiative ... and includes" opens the class, and an ending that is neither at the employer's initiative nor a resignation is not said to be outside it
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 2(1) Interpretation: places, things and the Acts it points to`

-- src:572 | “place of employment” means any place provided by the
-- src:573 | employer where work is carried on, for or on behalf of an
-- src:574 | employer, by an employee;
@ref s 2(1) "place of employment" (src:572-574)
GIVEN `the place is provided by the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `work is carried on there, for or on behalf of an employer, by an employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "place of employment" the place is one` MEANS
    IF `the place is provided by the employer` AND `work is carried on there, for or on behalf of an employer, by an employee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any place provided by the employer where work is carried on, for or on behalf of an employer, by an employee"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:565 | “no-pay leave”, for an employee, means leave of absence
-- src:566 | without pay granted by the employer at the request of the
-- src:567 | employee;
@ref s 2(1) "no-pay leave" (src:565-567)
GIVEN `it is leave of absence without pay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is granted by the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is granted at the request of the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "no-pay leave" the leave is no-pay leave` MEANS
    IF `it is leave of absence without pay` AND `it is granted by the employer` AND `it is granted at the request of the employee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means leave of absence without pay granted by the employer at the request of the employee"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- "Quarters" is a building provided for a workman to live in, with the rooms and
-- buildings for cooking, eating, washing or bathing and the latrines and urinals
-- added.
-- src:598 | “quarters” means any building provided or intended to be
-- src:599 | provided for a workman to live in either temporarily or
-- src:600 | permanently, and includes any room or building used or
-- src:601 | intended to be used whether communally or privately for the
-- src:602 | purposes of cooking, eating, washing or bathing and any
-- src:603 | latrines and urinals;
@ref s 2(1) "quarters" (src:598-603)
GIVEN `it is a building provided or intended to be provided for a workman to live in, temporarily or permanently` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a room or building used or intended to be used, communally or privately, for cooking, eating, washing or bathing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a latrine or urinal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "quarters" the building is quarters` MEANS
    IF `it is a building provided or intended to be provided for a workman to live in, temporarily or permanently` OR `it is a room or building used or intended to be used, communally or privately, for cooking, eating, washing or bathing` OR `it is a latrine or urinal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "means any building provided or intended to be provided for a workman to live in ... and includes" opens the class
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The things the definition lists, by name.
-- src:536 | “machinery” includes all oil engines, gas engines, steam engines
-- src:537 | and any other machines in which mechanical movement,
-- src:538 | either linear or rotated or both, takes place, steam boilers, gas
-- src:543 | cylinders, air receivers, steam receivers, steam containers,
-- src:544 | cast iron underfired vulcanizers, refrigerating plants, pressure
-- src:545 | receivers, all appliances for the transmission of power by
-- src:546 | ropes, belts, chains, driving straps or bands or gearing,
-- src:547 | electrical generators and electrical motors;
@ref s 2(1) "machinery" (src:536-547)
DECLARE `s 2(1) "machinery" Kind of thing` IS ONE OF
    `s 2(1) "machinery" an oil engine`
    `s 2(1) "machinery" a gas engine`
    `s 2(1) "machinery" a steam engine`
    `s 2(1) "machinery" any other machine in which mechanical movement, linear or rotated or both, takes place`
    `s 2(1) "machinery" a steam boiler`
    `s 2(1) "machinery" a gas cylinder`
    `s 2(1) "machinery" an air receiver`
    `s 2(1) "machinery" a steam receiver`
    `s 2(1) "machinery" a steam container`
    `s 2(1) "machinery" a cast iron underfired vulcanizer`
    `s 2(1) "machinery" a refrigerating plant`
    `s 2(1) "machinery" a pressure receiver`
    `s 2(1) "machinery" an appliance for the transmission of power by ropes, belts, chains, driving straps or bands or gearing`
    `s 2(1) "machinery" an electrical generator`
    `s 2(1) "machinery" an electrical motor`
    `s 2(1) "machinery" something not in the list`

@ref s 2(1) "machinery" (src:536-547)
GIVEN thing IS A `s 2(1) "machinery" Kind of thing`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "machinery" the thing is machinery` MEANS
    IF thing EQUALS `s 2(1) "machinery" something not in the list`
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes all oil engines, gas engines, steam engines and any other machines" lists things that are machinery and does not close the list
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- "Industrial undertaking" means undertakings in general, public and private, and
-- includes four named kinds.  Read literally, any undertaking is one (NOTES.md,
-- fork F3).
-- src:512 | “industrial undertaking” means public and private undertakings
-- src:513 | and any branch thereof, and includes particularly —
-- src:515 | (a) mines, quarries and other works for the extraction of
-- src:516 | minerals from the earth;
-- src:518 | (b) undertakings in which articles are manufactured,
-- src:519 | assembled, altered, cleaned, repaired, ornamented,
-- src:520 | finished, adapted for sale, broken up or demolished,
-- src:521 | or in which materials are transformed, including
-- src:522 | undertakings engaged in shipbuilding, or in the
-- src:523 | generation, transformation or transmission of
-- src:524 | electricity or motive power of any kind;
-- src:526 | (c) undertakings engaged in constructional work; and
-- src:528 | (d) undertakings engaged in the transport of passengers
-- src:529 | or goods by road, rail, sea, inland waterway or air,
-- src:530 | including the handling of goods at docks, quays,
-- src:531 | wharves, warehouses or airports;
@ref s 2(1) "industrial undertaking" (src:512-531)
GIVEN `it is an undertaking, public or private, or a branch of one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a mine, quarry or other work for the extraction of minerals from the earth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an undertaking in which articles are manufactured, assembled, altered, cleaned, repaired, ornamented, finished, adapted for sale, broken up or demolished, or materials are transformed, including shipbuilding and the generation, transformation or transmission of electricity or motive power of any kind` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an undertaking engaged in constructional work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an undertaking engaged in the transport of passengers or goods by road, rail, sea, inland waterway or air, including the handling of goods at docks, quays, wharves, warehouses or airports` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "industrial undertaking" the undertaking is one` MEANS
    IF `it is an undertaking, public or private, or a branch of one` OR `it is a mine, quarry or other work for the extraction of minerals from the earth` OR `it is an undertaking in which articles are manufactured, assembled, altered, cleaned, repaired, ornamented, finished, adapted for sale, broken up or demolished, or materials are transformed, including shipbuilding and the generation, transformation or transmission of electricity or motive power of any kind` OR `it is an undertaking engaged in constructional work` OR `it is an undertaking engaged in the transport of passengers or goods by road, rail, sea, inland waterway or air, including the handling of goods at docks, quays, wharves, warehouses or airports`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "means public and private undertakings and any branch thereof, and includes particularly" opens the class
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 2(1) Interpretation: what the definitions point to outside the Act or in another part`

-- A pointer to another Act.  Its test is not among the sources: the fact is asked,
-- and an unknown answer (NOTHING) is passed on.
-- src:387 | “collective agreement” means an agreement as defined under the
-- src:388 | Industrial Relations Act 1960;
@ref s 2(1) "collective agreement" (src:387-388)
GIVEN `it is an agreement as defined under the Industrial Relations Act 1960` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "collective agreement" the agreement is one` MEANS
    CONSIDER `it is an agreement as defined under the Industrial Relations Act 1960`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the test is in the Industrial Relations Act 1960, which is not among the sources
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST isOne THEN
        IF isOne THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means an agreement as defined under the Industrial Relations Act 1960"
        ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:549 | “mediation request” has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the
-- src:550 | Employment Claims Act 2016;
@ref s 2(1) "mediation request" (src:549-550)
GIVEN `it is a mediation request within the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Employment Claims Act 2016` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "mediation request" the request is one` MEANS
    CONSIDER `it is a mediation request within the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Employment Claims Act 2016`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the meaning is given by the Employment Claims Act 2016, which is not among the sources
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST isOne THEN
        IF isOne THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Employment Claims Act 2016"
        ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:650 | “stillborn child” has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the
-- src:651 | Registration of Births and Deaths Act 2021;
@ref s 2(1) "stillborn child" (src:650-651)
GIVEN `it is a stillborn child within the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Registration of Births and Deaths Act 2021` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "stillborn child" the child is one` MEANS
    CONSIDER `it is a stillborn child within the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Registration of Births and Deaths Act 2021`
