§ `Employment Act 1968 -- Part 1 Preliminary, ss 3, 5 and 6`

§§ `s 3(1) Appointment of officers`

-- The Deputy Commissioner and the two ranks of Assistant Commissioner may perform
-- the Commissioner's duties and exercise the Commissioner's powers, subject to
-- limitations that may be prescribed, and what they do is deemed duly done.  What
-- it means for a person dealt with by such an officer: the act counts as the
-- Commissioner's.  Ss 3(2) to 3(4) (the appointment of officers) are staffing and
-- are not encoded (NOTES.md).
-- src:719 | 3.—(1) The Minister may appoint an officer as the Commissioner
-- src:720 | for Labour (called in this Act the Commissioner) and also one or
-- src:721 | more officers as Deputy Commissioner for Labour, Principal
-- src:722 | Assistant Commissioner for Labour or Assistant Commissioner for
-- src:723 | Labour, who, subject to such limitations as may be prescribed, may
-- src:724 | perform all duties imposed and exercise all powers conferred on the
-- src:725 | Commissioner by this Act, and every duty so performed and power so
-- src:726 | exercised is deemed to have been duly performed and exercised for
-- src:727 | the purposes of this Act.
@ref s 3(1) (src:719-727)
GIVEN officer IS AN `Official or body the Act names`
      `a limitation prescribed under section 3(1) applies to the duty or power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(1) the officer's performance of the Commissioner's duty or exercise of the Commissioner's power is deemed duly done` MEANS
    CONSIDER officer
    WHEN `Official: a Deputy Commissioner, Principal Assistant Commissioner or Assistant Commissioner for Labour` THEN
        IF `a limitation prescribed under section 3(1) applies to the duty or power`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to such limitations as may be prescribed"
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 3(1) deals with the Commissioner and the three ranks of deputy and assistant, and says nothing of any other official
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

